  {
    "episode_id": 42576,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/4/2/42576.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 29,
    "turn_text": "Those working at our prisons are among Ohio's frontline heroes. We thank them very, very much for their work. For a sad report that COVID-19 has taken the life of another member of the Ohio Department of Rehabilitation and Corrections family. Bernard Atta had been a nurse at the Correctional Reception Center in Orient since December of 2012. He'd been off work since May 8th after showing symptoms of COVID-19. He subsequently tested positive. He was just 61 years old. He died at his home yesterday morning. Our condolences go out to his family and to his colleagues. I've asked DRC Director and Netchamber Smith to join us today to give us kind of an update. She did this several weeks ago, but to discuss the latest measures underway in our prisons and how things are going. Director, thank you for joining us.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_13",
