    "episode_id": 42576,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/4/2/42576.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 42,
    "turn_text": "Okay. So PPE, yes. Now we have enough surgical masks on hand to give a mask for every shift to every person who works inside the prison. And of course, the people that live in the prison have four cloth masks that they rotate and clean. And then we replace because they're only good for 15 washes. I think that the problem with PPE and the reason you hear so much about it is because not everyone agrees on what type of PPE should be used under what circumstance. And we follow CDC guidelines in a department. I feel it's important to have some kind of authority, give us guidelines that tell us what to do when, because everyone has an opinion about what ought to be happening. And I think we should use the expert's opinion and make sure that we implement it across the board faithfully. That's probably the best that we can do at this point.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_07",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
