    "turn_text": "an expansion of an already existing group that is in public safety under Tom Stickrath. I asked the team to take a look at this, and they decided to take the normal group. Laura, I'll have to check on the number. But the normal group, excuse me, is 70 people. That doesn't mean they're all deployed at the same time. They would not be. And we're going to increase that. And frankly, I don't know yet how big a group that will be. The truth is that we rely, frankly, on good behavior in most things. Most laws, most regulations, is people doing what they're supposed to be doing. And enforcement is not the way that behavior takes place. But, frankly, this is so very, very important that we get this right that we're going to increase the normal enforcement. We'll be able to tell you in a few days how many people will be involved. There's really two types of enforcement. One has to do with a filing under the criminal section. The other has to do with an administrative citation. I think this weekend, for example, there were several citations issued, one in Medway, Ohio, in Clark County. There was one issued in Columbus by this state group. In addition to that, though, you also have local health departments. And we have not gotten in the full reports of every health department around the state. I think I was told this morning at Columbus issued eight citations, their health department. But I don't have the numbers for the other cities. But that's separate from what I'm talking about. You have the health department enforcement, then you've got the group under public safety, the special investigation unit.",
