  {
    "episode_id": 42576,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/4/2/42576.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 63,
    "turn_text": "Individuals can be cited. Absolutely individuals can be cited. We would not rule that out at all. Look, Jim, I think that we're all going through this in a learning process. You know, it's nice outside. People want to get out. They haven't had the opportunity to go to a restaurant, go to a bar. Now they're taking that opportunity, and absolutely nothing wrong with that at all. But again, this virus is still here. This virus has not gone away. The facts have simply not changed. And so if we are going to open up the economy, If we're going to get Ohioans back to work, we've got to do it in a responsible way. We've got to do it in a way that keeps people safe. Because if we go off the rails here, if we go off the rails and we're not keeping people safe and we're seeing there are not number, for example, Dr. Acton was talking about. We see that start creeping up above 1, 1.1, 1.2. alarm bells need to go off. And we're going to do what we have to do to protect Ohioans. We're not going to let us surge in regard to this. So, again, this is a very delicate operation. This is a high risk, but it's a risk if we didn't do anything. And so to my fellow high ones who, you know, at least by the pictures, didn't look like they thought that this remains a threat. Let me just say it is a threat. And if you are not worried about yourself, you should worry about your mom, your dad, your grandparents, you should worry about strangers who somehow might get it from you. This is A case in your life and it may be the only time in your life we hope were literally what you do every day and how you practice good, common sense, keeping six feet away, wearing a mask, that is going to determine whether people live or die. Very few times in our life, maybe never. Are we faced in a situation where we're doing something that can cause someone else their life? And I don't think there's any of us. There's any of us that when we really think about it want to do something that causes someone else to die or someone else if they don't die to be sick as we heard today for two weeks or excuse me two months on her back in the hospital. So there's a lot of stake we can do this but to my fellow high ones have fun, but you know, keep that distance. When you go to the restaurant, you go the bar, sit down. That's what the regulations say. That way you can ensure that there is a space in there and that there is in fact a distance. Thank you.",
