    "turn_text": "have to do to keep the spread down. But I truly believe that Ohioans, as they look at this, more and more Ohioans will be wearing masks. This is something that you don't do for yourself, but you do it for someone else. I know that there's some Ohioans that maybe have a physical reason they can't wear those, and that's fine. But for everybody else, this is something that we do for everyone else. And this is something that we do to protect others. And it is an additional layer. It's not a substitute, not a substitute for distance. Distance, map. mask, distance mask, makes a difference. And I think you're going to continue to see the numbers of our fellow Ohioans who are wearing these go up as they understand really what's at stake. What's at stake is lives. What's at stake is keeping other people from getting sick. And for those Ohioans who say, well, I'm not sick. But we know from now, empirically, from testing is there's a lot of people who walk around and they are carrying the virus and they have no idea they're carrying the virus. And so as Dr. Atkins said, we should assume everybody that we come in contact with has the virus. And if we act that way, then we will slow this down. I'm optimistic. Look, people are going to continue to do this at a higher rate every week.",
