  {
    "episode_id": 42576,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/4/2/42576.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 85,
    "turn_text": "Very important. We did hit 10,000 a couple of days ago. We're now averaging over 9,000 a day. I noticed in an article over the weekend that I read that we're not the only state that is not at capacity. There are a lot of states that are having that. But we have two jobs to do. When I told my team this again this morning, we have two jobs to do. One is to close that gap. And what the challenge has been, we basically have a capacity, what I will call machine capacity at one level. That machine capacity shortly is going to be at 22,000 per day. That machine capacity is there, but what we're doing is we're building out It's never been built before. We're building out a supply chain and distribution chain for swabs and everything else connected with that testing. And so we're focusing on that. The other thing, Andy, that we're focused on is at the same time taking that capacity even higher. Because we know we're going to fill this up. We're going to keep going up and up and up and up. But we know that 22,000 a day is not where we need to be. We know that we have to be even beyond that. So two different functions, two different things going on. Our team is working every single day to make this happen.",
