    "turn_idx": 91,
    "turn_text": "Let me just summarize. Our goal is to get as much testing in this state as we can. We're working on every single day. The other thing we're doing is to deploy that, and my charge to our team is deploy the testing we have in a targeted way, most effective way. So doing two things, trying to raise that testing every single day, number of tests, but it's not enough just to raise the testing. and just go out and test willy-nilly. It's important to take whatever capacity that is and to target that in the place where we can save the most lives. So I'm not satisfied with where we are. We got to do more. We've come a long way, but we have a long way to go. And so we understand the danger. I understand the danger to people in nursing homes. I understand the danger to people in any kind or good setting. Eric has given me the word here to close. Let me end with a song by central Ohio band McGuffie Lane. Songs called Times Like These. Let's take a listen.",
